		<h1>Web Site Critiques</h1>


		<h3> Evaluation Questions</h3> 

		<ol> 
			<li> What was your first impression of this site?</li>
			<li> How does this site organize the flow of information?</li>
			<li> Does the site structure make sense or does it confuse you? Why? </li> 
			<li> Does the site graphics/layout/multimedia enhance the site or detract from it? Why?</li>
			<li> How long did it take for the home page to load? Was the load time reasonable?</li>
			<li> Was the text color and size readable? If a background color or image was used, did it enhance or detract from the site?</li>
			<li> Did the site have a navigation bar or other navigation tool? Was the navigation well done?</li>
			<li> Did the site have a color scheme or look and feel that was repeated on all the pages?</li>
			<li> How does the site respond to smaller window sizes (responsive design)?</li>
			<li> What does this site offer that was unusual or very well done?</li>
		</ol>
		
		<h2> Site Evaluation: [TRADER JOE'S]</h2>
		<p><strong>URL: </strong> <a href="https://www.traderjoes.com/home">Trader Joe's Home Page</a></p>
		
		<h3> My Critique</h3>
		<p>1. [My first impression is that it has visual design and branding. It also has content and layout.] </p>
		<p>2. [It has a title of All the Fall Things. It has Welcome to Trader Joe's!] </p>
		<p>3. [The structure makes sense because its giving you different recipes to try to make.] </p>
		<p>4. [The first graphic is a picture of TRADER JOE's (inside), the second one says WE COME BEARING FALL, a leaf, a mushroom, a spiral, a fork, then a little animal.] </p>
		<p>5. [The load time was fast and I found it reasonable.] </p>
		<p>6. [The text color is black and some red, the size is readable, and the back ground is white.] </p>
		<p>7. [There are two arrows going left and right. There is a podcast ":Expect the Unexpected (Cheddar) at Trader Joe's.] </p>
		<p>8. [The color scheme and stylying are consistent for the other pages.] </p>
		<p>9. [The responsiveness is you can resize the browser size and see if anything changes.] </p>
		<p>10. [There is something like a camera on the website and there is believe eat or not recipes.] </p>

